# MITRE ATT&CK T1053.005 — Scheduled Task

## ATT&CK Reference

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Tactic | Persistence |
| Technique | Scheduled Task/Job |
| Sub-technique | Scheduled Task |
| Technique ID | T1053.005 |
| Lab Detection | DET-004 — Suspicious Scheduled Task Creation |
| Primary Telemetry | Windows Endpoint Telemetry |
| SIEM | Splunk Enterprise |
| Status | Validated |

Official MITRE ATT&CK reference:

[T1053.005 — Scheduled Task](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1053/005/)

---

# Technique Overview

Windows Scheduled Tasks provide a native mechanism for executing programs or commands according to defined triggers.

Legitimate uses include:

- System maintenance
- Application updates
- Backup operations
- Enterprise management
- Administrative automation

The same capability can also be used to execute commands or establish persistence.

Sprint 22 focuses on the observable behavior:

```text
schtasks.exe
      +
/create
```

DET-004 provides visibility into command-line scheduled-task creation.

---

