---

# Detection SPL

Validated detection concept:

```spl
index=* "schtasks.exe" "/create"
```

Host-specific validation:

```spl
index=* host="WIN11-02" "schtasks.exe" "/create"
```

Portfolio output:

```spl
index=* "schtasks.exe" "/create"
| eval detection="DET-004 - Suspicious Scheduled Task Creation"
| table _time detection host _raw
```

The detection intentionally uses fields and observable strings confirmed in the lab rather than relying on an assumed EventCode mapping.

---

# Controlled Validation

A benign scheduled task was created:

```cmd
schtasks /create /tn "Sprint22-DET004-Positive" /tr "cmd.exe /c echo DET004 Positive >> C:\Windows\Temp\DET004.txt" /sc once /st 23:59 /f
```

The task performed no harmful activity.

The objective was to reproduce scheduled-task creation behavior safely.

---

# Positive Test

```text
schtasks.exe
      |
      v
/create
      |
      v
New Scheduled Task
      |
      v
Endpoint Telemetry
      |
      v
Splunk
      |
      v
DET-004
      |
      v
TRIGGER
```

**Result:** PASS

---

# Negative Test

Normal task enumeration was performed:

```cmd
schtasks /query
```

This produced scheduled-task-related activity without creating a task.

```text
schtasks.exe
      |
      v
/query
      |
      v
No /create
      |
      v
DET-004
      |
      v
NO TRIGGER
```

**Result:** PASS

