```

---

# Detection vs. Threat Hunting

DET-004:

```text
schtasks.exe
     +
/create
     |
     v
Alert
```

Threat hunting:

```text
schtasks.exe
Register-ScheduledTask
Other Task Activity
     |
     v
Analyst Investigation
```

This allows broad visibility without generating excessive alerts.

---

# False Positive Analysis

Scheduled tasks are a normal Windows feature.

Potential false positives include:

```text
Operating System
      |
Software Installation
      |
Application Update
      |
Backup
      |
Monitoring
      |
Enterprise Management
      |
Administrator Automation
```

Therefore:

```text
Scheduled Task != Malicious
```

and:

```text
Scheduled Task Creation != Confirmed Persistence
```

Context determines severity.

---

# Detection Confidence Model

### Basic Signal

```text
Scheduled Task Creation
```

### Increased Confidence

```text
Scheduled Task Creation
        +
Unexpected User
```

### Higher Confidence

```text
Scheduled Task Creation
        +
Unexpected User
        +
Suspicious Action
        +
Privileged Execution
```

### Stronger Correlation

```text
Encoded PowerShell
        +
Scheduled Task Creation
        +
Suspicious Action
        +
Network Activity
        |
        v
Higher Investigative Priority
```

This demonstrates how individual behavioral detections can eventually become correlated SOC analytics.

---

# Telemetry Engineering Lesson

Sprint 22 also demonstrated the importance of validating SIEM schemas.

Initial investigation assumed:

```text
Sysmon Event ID 1
        =
Splunk EventCode=1
```

That assumption did not correctly identify the relevant task telemetry in the lab.

The successful workflow became:

```text
Generate Known Activity
       |
       v
Observe Endpoint
       |
       v
Search Splunk Broadly
       |
       v
Identify Actual Representation
       |
       v
Build Detection
```

This is a critical detection-engineering practice because SIEM field extraction can vary by:

- Input
- Sourcetype
- Parser
- Add-on
- Log format
- Forwarder configuration

Detections should therefore be validated against actual indexed telemetry.

